& [Purpose] is independent review evidence without pretending review is execution
  + establish what an exact case should mean before comparison
  + verify common claims and coverage edges
  + preserve challenges and uncertainty
  + form a reviewed corpus candidate only after complete faculty evidence

& [AuthorityState] is formation_only
  + no proposal catalogue review receipt reviewer principal trust entry key signature candidate or execution exists
  + zero requirements are implemented or verified

& [PrerequisiteIdentity] is exact
  + active immutable I03E1 obligation catalogue
  + active exact I03E2 proposal catalogue case payloads operator lineage and gaps
  + canonical I02 schemas actual Rust type sources I03B ingress I03C residual I03D reader and I03E report profiles
  + future trust policy reviewer catalogue faculty profiles code lock and review implementation identity
  + mismatch blocks review rather than creating a revised expectation silently

& [FourAuthorityLayers] are non-substitutive
  + ExpectationAuthority states reviewed intended result over exact case identity
  + ObservationAuthority records actual stage result under exact execution identity
  + ComparisonAuthority classifies preserved expectation and observation
  + AdmissionAuthority verifies complete evidence and grants only its explicitly signed next phase
  + no earlier layer can impersonate a later layer

& [IndependenceAxes] are declared
  + generator differs from expectation authority
  + implementation observation differs from oracle rationale
  + comparator preserves both inputs and differs from their authorship
  + review records principal run source and conflicts
  + integrity digest differs from attestation and signature

& [IndependenceClass] is closed
  + procedural_only uses separate faculty contracts but may share execution principal
  + separate_invocations uses distinct immutable review runs
  + separate_principals uses distinct authorized reviewer principals
  + future trust policy names the minimum class per case severity
  + a receipt states actual class and never infers a stronger class

& [ExpectationSource] is exact articulated meaning
  + case root direction payload operator and predecessor identity
  + stage-by-stage expected disposition and applicability
  + claim witness and obligation mapping propositions
  + cited schema pointer Rust source ingress clause residual record or resource boundary
  + exact arithmetic construction vector or non-invocation proof
  + observed output can motivate reconsideration but never becomes expectation merely by being observed

& [OracleClasses] are stage bound
  + byte oracle uses exact bytes spans decoded member identity JSON grammar and checked resource relations
  + schema oracle uses canonical rule sites Draft 2020-12 semantics and fixed validator profile
  + typed oracle uses actual Rust type serde attributes direction constructibility and representation
  + semantic oracle uses complete fixtures exact safe_pure contract and independently prepared vectors or derivations
  + authority oracle proves prohibited behavior was not invoked and grants no semantic authority
  + no f64 approximate projection is an exact boundary oracle

& [CaseExpectationReceipt] is complete
  + one exact case digest
  + ingress schema typed semantic comparison and applicability dispositions
  + oracle class evidence references bounded rationale reviewer run predecessor and digest
  + challenged or insufficient stages remain explicit

& [ClaimWitnessReceipt] validates comparison meaning
  + CommonSyntaxClaim proposition is coherent for selected root direction and case
  + schema witness and typed witness address the same proposition through their own vocabularies
  + expected accepted rejected or not-comparable result is justified for both sides
  + absence of a common proposition produces not_comparable rather than false agreement

& [CoverageMappingReceipt] validates one edge
  + binds exact case obligation edge behavior proposition disposition source and rationale
  + shared fixture template bytes or operator do not satisfy another root automatically
  + every multi-obligation case has individually listed edges
  + gaps survive review until exact successor evidence closes them

& [ReviewerPrincipal] is trust bound
  + kind person or faculty_process
  + stable principal id and trust policy
  + faculty process binds SOP profile engine or model identity job input output and run provenance
  + optional key id is explicit and never inferred from principal name
  + raw model prose without authorized principal and provenance has no receipt authority

& [TrustedReviewerCatalogue] is a future signed input
  + exact principal profiles allowed faculty roles independence groups keys algorithms validity and revocation state
  + catalogue digest and version bind every review run
  + unknown stale revoked mismatched or self-asserted entries refuse review
  + formation defines the form and creates no principal or key

& [IntegrityAttestationSignature] are distinct
  + IntegrityDigest is content-address identity
  + checksum or CRC is integrity detection with its named algorithm
  + Attestation binds principal faculty role disposition and protocol to one exact payload digest
  + DigitalSignature is cryptographic verification under declared algorithm key id trusted catalogue and signature bytes
  + no checksum digest or attestation is called a digital signature

& [FacultyPrimaryReview] is independent
  + HonestyPrimary reviews identity attribution source independence semantic claim truth scope and non-overclaim
  + SecurityPrimary reviews carrier bounds malformed containment immutable schemas no-resolution no effects construction and prohibited authority
  + each payload contains no peer payload digest
  + each has its own review run principal challenges disposition and integrity digest

& [TwoPhaseCrossConfirmation] is non-circular
  * form HonestyPrimaryPayload and SecurityPrimaryPayload independently
  * compute both primary digests
  * HonestyCrossAck inspects both primary payloads and binds both digests
  * SecurityCrossAck independently inspects both primary payloads and binds both digests
  * compute both acknowledgment digests
  * form CrossConfirmationEnvelope over two primary digests two acknowledgment digests principals independence class trust policy and combined disposition
  + no record includes its own digest or future envelope digest

& [CrossAcknowledgment] cannot usurp peer authority
  + Honesty acknowledges Security boundary evidence without issuing Security's conclusion
  + Security acknowledges Honesty identity evidence without issuing Honesty's conclusion
  + disagreement creates explicit challenge and blocks combined affirmation
  + combined disposition is affirmed only when both primaries and both acknowledgments affirm

& [OptionalCryptographicSignature] attaches after envelope digest
  + SignatureRecord names algorithm key id trusted catalogue digest signed envelope digest signature bytes digest verification and verifier
  + signature bytes are external to the signed payload and cannot create digest recursion
  + missing signature is represented honestly
  + future activation states whether verified signatures are mandatory

& [DissentLedger] is immutable
  + dispositions affirm challenge abstain and insufficient_evidence
  + exact subject clause evidence rationale severity and proposed resolution
  + open challenge abstention or insufficient evidence blocks the affected subject
  + resolution is a successor referencing original dissent and exact correction
  + deletion replacement or silent downgrade is forbidden

& [SuccessorRules] are causal
  + payload bytes fixture operator or parameters change Case identity and invalidate prior case receipts
  + stage expectation claim witness mapping or rationale change receipt identity
  + reviewer principal run or source basis change review identity
  + trust catalogue or independence-policy change requires requalification
  + successor chains retain every predecessor

& [BatchReview] reduces repeated rationale only
  + batch lists every exact case digest shared operator mapping expectation class source basis and rationale
  + each case has an explicit batch membership receipt edge
  + exceptions and dissent remain case-specific
  + changing batch basis invalidates all dependent edges
  + statistical sampling may audit review quality but never admits an unreviewed case

& [FacultyKernel] is observable
  * Scribe confirms immutable case payload provenance and reference completeness
  * Refiner confirms one-change lineage identity and normalized forms
  * Weaver confirms root claim obligation residual and template mappings
  * Planner confirms prerequisites constructibility dependency order and complete queue
  * Honesty and Security form independent primaries and cross acknowledgments
  * Observer verifies exact account totals envelope trust dissent closure and authority limit
  + only receipts claims evidence and bounded rationale are normative
  + private chain-of-thought is neither required nor proof

& [ObserverDisposition] is closed
  + review_not_ready means required subjects or trust evidence are absent
  + review_refused means a contradiction challenge policy or boundary fault remains
  + corpus_candidate_formed means all selected cases have complete affirmed review evidence and all gaps are honestly represented according to policy
  + corpus_candidate_formed grants no reader execution or conformance result

& [Completeness] is total not sampled
  + every admitted proposed case has one expectation receipt
  + every CommonSyntaxClaim has one witness receipt
  + every proposed obligation edge has one mapping receipt
  + every required faculty review and cross envelope exists
  + every dissent is open or resolved explicitly
  + checked accounts reconstruct completeness from records

& [ModelAssistance] is transparent
  + an LLM may propose rationale challenge or missing edge
  + retained provenance identifies model engine job immutable input and output digests
  + an authorized faculty process may become a ReviewerPrincipal only under explicit trust policy
  + raw suggestions alone cannot attest sign admit or suppress dissent

& [CanonicalEncoding] is deterministic
  + fixed field order lexical complete record ordering and domain-separated digests
  + normative payload excludes time host path thread order random state commentary and hidden reasoning
  + external provenance timestamps may exist outside normative identity
  + identical facts dispositions and trust inputs yield byte-identical payloads

& [Limits] are finite before review activation
  + exact maxima for cases receipts claims edges primary reviews acknowledgments envelopes signatures dissent successors batches references rationale and bytes
  + every join count traversal and allocation uses checked arithmetic
  + exhaustion leaves exact subjects unreviewed and prevents candidate formation

& [FutureSourceTouch] is unsigned
  + exact review forms and pure verifier location under I03E implementation inventory
  + compile-time trust policy reviewer catalogue and review catalogue fixtures
  + focused receipt envelope dissent successor batch and completeness tests
  + no key generation secret persistence runtime file database network provider model service or effect

& [Proof] after future activation includes
  + generator result-copy and comparator-rewrite self-confirmation adversaries
  + exact byte numeric schema typed semantic and authority oracle examples
  + distinct integrity attestation signature and trust failures
  + two primaries two acknowledgments non-circular envelope and disagreement
  + dissent successors batch invalidation complete-account and exhaustion
  + corpus candidate without reader execution proof

& [FormationBoundary] is strict
  + source SJS canonical exploded requirements justification plan review inactive lock proof narrative and evidence metadata only
  - never: receipt issuance trusted principal key creation digital signing corpus candidate execution reader semantic invocation compatibility admission provider model service persistence network effect production hardware FPGA or shared inference

& [Disposition] is canonical_formation_complete_review_issuance_refused
